333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1021 0 R
/T (industrial machines are increasingly equipped with sensors that continuously collect operational information. These sensors measure different parameters such as temperature, vibration, pressure, speed, and other machine-related readings. The collected information provides valuable insights into the operating condition of industrial equipment.)
/E (industrial machines are increasingly equipped with sensors that continuously collect operational information. These sensors measure different parameters such as temperature, vibration, pressure, speed, and other machine-related readings. The collected information provides valuable insights into the operating condition of industrial equipment.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1022 0 R
/E (However, a large amount of sensor data is generated during machine operation. Manually examining every reading is difficult and time-consuming. Therefore, intelligent data analysis techniques are required to automatically identify unusual patterns and detect possible machine abnormalities.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1023 0 R
/E (Deep Learning provides powerful techniques for analysing complex data and identifying patterns that may not be easily detected through traditional methods. One such technique is an Autoencoder, a neural network architecture that learns to represent and reconstruct input data. Autoencoders can be trained using normal machine sensor readings. After training, the model attempts to reconstruct new sensor readings. If the input data contains unusual patterns, the reconstruction error may become significantly higher than the error observed for normal operating conditions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
