/P 200 0 R
/T (Problem Statement )
/E (Problem Statement )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 200 0 R
/T (In modern industries, machines are continuously used for manufacturing, production, and various industrial operations. The efficient functioning of these machines is essential for maintaining productivity, reducing operational costs, and ensuring safety. However, industrial machines are exposed to different operating conditions that may lead to abnormal behaviour, performance degradation, and unexpected failures.)
/E (In modern industries, machines are continuously used for manufacturing, production, and various industrial operations. The efficient functioning of these machines is essential for maintaining productivity, reducing operational costs, and ensuring safety. However, industrial machines are exposed to different operating conditions that may lead to abnormal behaviour, performance degradation, and unexpected failures.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Machine sensors generate large amounts of data related to operational parameters such as temperature, vibration, speed, pressure, and other machine-related measurements. These sensor readings contain important information about the condition and performance of machines. However, analysing this large volume of data manually is difficult, time-consuming, and inefficient.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Traditional machine monitoring systems generally depend on predefined threshold values, periodic inspections, or manual observation. Such approaches may fail to identify complex abnormal patterns, particularly when the relationship between different sensor parameters is nonlinear or changes over time. In addition, unexpected machine abnormalities may not always be detected before they result in equipment failure or production interruption.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 201 0 R
/T (Therefore, there is a need for an intelligent and automated system that can analyse machine sensor readings, learn normal operating behaviour, and identify unusual patterns that may indicate abnormal machine conditions.)
/E (Therefore, there is a need for an intelligent and automated system that can analyse machine sensor readings, learn normal operating behaviour, and identify unusual patterns that may indicate abnormal machine conditions.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
