349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1027 0 R
/E (The project also aims to perform effective preprocessing of machine sensor data before applying the deep learning model. Raw sensor data may contain missing values, duplicate records, noise, and variations in the numerical ranges of different parameters. Therefore, an objective of the project is to prepare the data in a suitable format for model training and evaluation. The use of data cleaning, normalisation, and sliding-window techniques helps in improving the consistency and suitability of the sensor data. Min-Max Scaling is used to transform sensor readings into a common numerical range, while the sliding-window approach is used to organise the data into sequences of 30 readings for processing by the Autoencoder architecture.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
